{title: 155 - When I Survey the Wondrous Cross}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #155 • ROCKINGHAM  OLD • 16.16}
{lyricist: Isaac Watts}
{composer: Edward Miller}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 155}
{meta: tune ROCKINGHAM  OLD}
{meta: meter 16.16}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]When I [Em/B]survey [D/A]the [A]wondrous [D]cross On [Bm]which [A#m]the [C#dim]Prince [D]of [A]glory [D/A]died,
[A]My richest gain [D/A]Icount [Bm]but [A]loss, [G]And pour [D/A]contempt [Bm]on all [D/A]my [Em/G]pride.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]See, [Em/G]from [Bm]His [D/F#]head, [Bm]His [A7]feet,
[D/F#]Sorrow [A]and [D]love [Bm]flow [C#dim]mingled [A7]down;
[A]Did [G#m]e'er [D/A]such [Bm]love [G]and [D/A]sorrow meet?
[A]Or [G#m]thorns [D/A]compose [G]so [D/A]rich [Bm]a [D/A]crown?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]Since [Em/B]I, [D/A]who [Bm]was [D/F#]undone and lost,
[D/F#]Have [Em/B]pardon [Bm]through [D/F#]His [A#m]name [D]and word;
[A]Forbid [D/A]it, [Bm]then, [G]that [D/A]I [Bm]should [D/A]boast,
[A]Save [G#m]in [D/A]the [Bm]cross [G]of [D/A]Christ [Bm]my [D/A]Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D/F#]Were [Em/B]the [D/F#]whole realm [Bm]of nature [D/A]mine,
[D/F#]That [Em/B]were [D/A]a [Bm]tribute [A#m]far [D]too small;
[A]Love [G#m]so [D/A]amazing, so [Bm]divine,
[A]Demands [D/A]my [Bm]life, [G]my [D/A]soul, [Bm]my [D/A]all.
{end_of_verse}
